摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"AI agents for pentesting, code audit, fuzzing, vulnerability discovery, and reverse engineering: harnesses, sandboxes, security MCP servers, benchmarks, and evals.","id":"gh:1321115089","install_available":false,"language":null,"name":"awesome-security-agent-harnesses","slug":"Ed-Marcavage/awesome-security-agent-harnesses","topics":["agentic-ai","ai-agents","ai-hacking","ai-pentesting","ai-security","awesome","awesome-list","claude-code","cybersecurity","dsh","dsh-plugin","ethical-hacking","fuzzing","llm-security","mcp","offensive-security","penetration-testing","pentesting","reverse-engineering","security-automation"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"AI agents for pentesting, code audit, fuzzing, vulnerability discovery, and reverse engineering: har"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"nesses, sandboxes, security MCP servers, benchmarks, and evals."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# Awesome Security Agent Harnesses [](https://awesome.re) [](https://discord.gg/vkVn2xEQn)"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"> AI agents for pentesting, code audit, fuzzing, vulnerability discovery, and reverse engineering: h"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"arnesses, sandboxes, security MCP servers, benchmarks, and evals."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"**Explore the papers, code, and people behind security agents.** Which papers and benchmarks should "},{"id":"p4s2","text":"ers, code, and people behind security agents.** Which papers and benchmarks should you explore next?"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"This list is a starting point. I built Papers With Code Cyber to make the wider collection easier to"},{"id":"p5s2","text":" explore: cybersecurity papers, engineering posts, and repositories you can filter by topic, target,"},{"id":"p5s3","text":" and contribution—with organizations and developers connected to their work."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Built on Hugging Face’s open-source Papers with Code, focused on cybersecurity agent harnesses."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Watch the full 55-second demo"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"**Explore the live catalog →** · Connect your agent through MCP — no account or API key required."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"**Open source & contributions**"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"- **Suggest a paper, post, or repository:** contribute to this awesome list or request a catalog add"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"ition.\n- **Improve the tools:** bugs, feature requests, and PRs welcome in the website/API and MCP/C"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"ve the tools:** bugs, feature requests, and PRs welcome in the website/API and MCP/CLI repositories."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Please read the contribution guidelines before opening a pull request."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Building or studying security agent harnesses? Join the Discord to trade notes, benchmark results, a"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"tudying security agent harnesses? Join the Discord to trade notes, benchmark results, and new finds."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Contents"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"- What Is a Security Agent Harness\n- Code Audit Harnesses\n- Pentesting Agents\n- Fuzzing and Vulnerab"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"ility Discovery\n- DARPA AIxCC Cyber Reasoning Systems\n- Agent Tooling and Integrations\n- Agent Sandb"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"oxes\n- Benchmarks and Evals\n- Readings"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## What Is a Security Agent Harness"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"A security agent harness is everything wrapped around the model: the sandbox it runs in, the analysi"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"s tools it can call, the prompts and skills that encode a methodology, and the evals you use to chec"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"k it. Most of the engineering lives here rather than in the model, or as Cloudflare put it after sca"},{"id":"p16s4","text":"ling one across its own fleet, the harness is the bit that lasts."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Agents are good at producing plausible findings and bad at telling which ones are real. An agent wil"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"l edit the source so its own exploit works, then report the bug it just created. So the metric that "},{"id":"p17s3","text":"matters is not recall, which nobody can measure without already knowing every bug in a codebase, but"},{"id":"p17s4","text":" how few unconfirmed findings reach a human: Cloudflare's pipeline cut 20,799 raw candidates down to"},{"id":"p17s5","text":" 12,057 that survived validation, then folded away another 5,442 as duplicates. A harness that can r"},{"id":"p17s6","text":"eproduce a crash, replay an input, or re-run a static analyzer is how you throw out the bad ones bef"},{"id":"p17s7","text":"ore a human ever sees them."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Entries tagged `SKILL.md` are skill packs rather than runnable harnesses: methodology encoded as Age"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"nt Skills that a general coding agent like Claude Code executes. They live in the section matching w"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"at a general coding agent like Claude Code executes. They live in the section matching what they do."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## Code Audit Harnesses"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Harnesses that run coding agents against source code: discovery, triage, validation, and patching."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"- 0 Security - Security harness with a local web console for vulnerability research, verification, a"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"nd fixes, exposing the same reusable workflows through CLI and MCP.\n- Anthropic Defending Code Refer"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"ence Harness - Reference implementation for autonomous vulnerability discovery and remediation with "},{"id":"p21s4","text":"Claude, with skills for threat modeling, scanning, triage, and patching.\n- audit - Eight-stage disco"},{"id":"p21s5","text":"very agent built on the Claude Code SDK, combining many narrow agents, deliberate disagreement betwe"},{"id":"p21s6","text":"en them, and an explicit reachability gate.\n- Capital One VulnHunter - Agentic security tool applyin"},{"id":"p21s7","text":"g proactive, attacker-first analysis directly to source code.\n- Clearwing - Autonomous source-code h"},{"id":"p21s8","text":"unter that ranks files, fans out specialist agents, and treats sanitizer crashes as ground truth, wi"},{"id":"p21s9","text":"th a separate network-pentest mode.\n- Cloudflare Security Audit - Six-phase audit skill: parallel hu"},{"id":"p21s10","text":"nting agents attack the codebase from different angles, separate agents try to disprove each finding"},{"id":"p21s11","text":", and fresh agents verify the schema-validated `findings.json` against source. `SKILL.md`.\n- Google "},{"id":"p21s12","text":"Mantis - Modular, stack-agnostic toolkit of security review skills for coding agents to find, reprod"},{"id":"p21s13","text":"uce, and patch vulnerabilities, with gVisor-sandboxed reproducers and an explicit false-positive fil"},{"id":"p21s14","text":"ter rule.\n- Krait - Claude Code audit methodology for Solidity with 101 heuristics, 26 analysis modu"},{"id":"p21s15","text":"les, and 8 kill gates that try to disprove every finding, measured blind on 50 Code4rena contests at"},{"id":"p21s16","text":" 100% precision on the v8 baseline.\n- Open Kritt - Self-hosted orchestrator that runs agents to find"},{"id":"p21s17","text":" and validate vulnerabilities, export canonical findings, and rank severity, with bug-bounty payouts"},{"id":"p21s18","text":" credited to its Blockian researcher identity.\n- OpenAI Codex Security - CLI and TypeScript SDK for "},{"id":"p21s19","text":"finding, validating, and fixing security vulnerabilities with Codex.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Pentesting Agents"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Agents that attack running applications and infrastructure: reconnaissance, exploitation, and proof "},{"id":"p23s2","text":"t attack running applications and infrastructure: reconnaissance, exploitation, and proof of impact."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"- AIDA - Model-agnostic pentesting agent that reasons over a defined scope, executes in an isolated "},{"id":"p24s2","text":"container, and keeps persistent assessment state across sessions.\n- AWE - Research framework pairing"},{"id":"p24s3","text":" a lightweight orchestration layer with memory-augmented, vulnerability-specific agent pipelines, ev"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"aluated on the XBOW benchmark.\n- BlacksmithAI - Multi-agent pentesting framework that walks a target"},{"id":"p24s5","text":" from reconnaissance through post-exploitation inside a Docker image preloaded with standard securit"},{"id":"p24s6","text":"y tooling, driven from either a web UI or a CLI.\n- BreachWeave - Multi-role pentest harness where a "},{"id":"p24s7","text":"Manager schedules and reclaims Solvers that exploit in parallel while a bystander Observer watches f"},{"id":"p24s8","text":"or drift and holds the termination decision, built on the Pi SDK; placed first of 613 teams in both "},{"id":"p24s9","text":"the online and offline rounds of the second Tencent Cloud AI pentest challenge.\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
